    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d26">

                <pb facs="d26-01" n="1" xml:id="d26-01"/>

                <head>26. Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                    (Kissinger) to Secretary of State Rogers<anchor n="1" xml:id="d26-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d26-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1971-07-13">July 13, 1971</date>
                </dateline>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT:</label>
                    <item> FPC Request for State Department Views on Natural Gas Imports from
                        Algeria</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President has approved your recommendation of June 25, 1971 and authorizes
                    you to respond favorably to the Federal Power Commission’s request for views on
                    applications to import gas from Algeria.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>Henry A. Kissinger </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d26-a1.xml" xpointer="d26-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d26-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d26-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials, NSC Files, Box 735,
                    Country Files, Africa, Algeria, Vol. I. Secret. While the tabs are not printed,
                    Tab B is summarized in the footnote to <ref target="#d24">Document 24</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d26-f2" n="2" xml:id="d26-f2-content">
                <p>With this memorandum Kissinger conveyed the President’s authorization to respond
                    favorably to the Federal Power Commission’s request for the administration’s
                    views on the importation of gas from Algeria and transmitted a memorandum
                    detailing the Algerian expropriation of United States and French property.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
